WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.800
This past week, former

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.334
Vice President

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.002
Mike Pence

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.870
testified more than 5 hours

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.238
before a federal grand jury

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.573
investigating the aftermath of

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.241
2020 election

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:08.942
is the highest

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.976
ranking government official

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.678
to take part in special counsel

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.113
Jack Smith's investigation

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.181
and conservative lawyer George Conway

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.883
joins us to talk about this.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.918
George great to see you as always.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.387
What do you think I mean,

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.589
what is your sense of Pence

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.858
spending 5 hours

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.259
before this federal grand jury.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:26.760
I mean you

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.228
you know how some of these cases

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.529
may play out.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.096
Could it have been

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.631
just I'm not commenting.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.166
I take the Fifth the whole time.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.868
This sounds as though he did offer

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.735
some information.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.972
Yeah, I doubt he did that for 5 hours.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.241
Not answering questions.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.742
I mean, it was litigated

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.544
all the way up to the US Court of Appeals

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.579
in the District of Columbia Circuit.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.682
And it's clear that he had testimony

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.150
to give.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.684
It's just a remarkable thing

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.952
historically as well,

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.821
because I don't think

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:55.722
I don't think

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.057
we've ever seen a circumstance

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.625
where a vice president

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.259
a former vice

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.162
president, is being called to testify

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.496
before a federal grand jury

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.098
in a criminal investigation

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:05.832
against the former

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.834
president under which he served

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.502
it simply a remarkable thing.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.937
And obviously

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.540
the court of Appeals rejected.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.242
Given what we can see from

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.911
from the sealed from the docket,

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.212
although most of all,

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.146
the papers are sealed

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:20.880
and the opinion is,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.314
you know,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.283
it's pretty clear the court of Appeals

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.218
rejected any effort

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.487
by Trump to block the testimony.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.989
And I think I hope

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.057
that that Mike Pence

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.026
was cooperative and testified.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.928
So all his conversations,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.296
which with the president,

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.263
which aren't subject

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.298
to executive privilege

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.666
because they weren't

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.968
in furtherance of Trump's

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.869
executive duties,

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.571
they were actually interrogation

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.572
of his duty

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.807
to support and defend the Constitution

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:48.775
You know,

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.877
I want to ask you about some of the other

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.012
legal issues facing the former president.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.614
But I have to ask you about this.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:55.615
Your Trump was photographed

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.449
this past week

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.451
hugging a woman who was sentenced to jail

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.920
for rioting at the Capitol

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.122
on January six,

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.457
calling for Pence to be executed.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.160
You know, he continues.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.095
Trump continues to escalate his support

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.730
for people charged in the Capitol riot.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.765
He's talked about pardoning some of them.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.933
What was your reaction to that

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.368
when you saw that?

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.305
Well, I'm really at a loss for words

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.774
whenever he does things like this,

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.443
because it's just continually

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.513
you think he's reached the bottom And yet

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.781
he seems somehow to dig himself

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.683
deeper into the muck.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.618
I mean, this is just

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.454
an absolute positive disgrace.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.623
He signed the woman's backpack

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.024
like it was some kind of souvenir,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.725
the backpack

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.027
she took to the insurrection

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.061
at the Capitol.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.863
He's clean, he's promising.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.098
He's been promising for months.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.032
That he's going to pardon

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.901
all these people, these people,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.769
hundreds of people who committed,

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.036
you know,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.904
real crimes

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.372
that they're being convicted for

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.840
and being sentenced for

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.408
in the District of Columbia.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.709
In the federal courts there.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.577
It's a complete

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.013
and utter disgrace and a disgrace

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.115
that anybody could support a man

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.018
who was who who swore an oath

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.586
to preserve, protect

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.021
and defend the Constitution,

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.956
the United States, who was the chief

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.124
law enforcement officer

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.325
in the United States, in effect,

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.460
because he's charged with executing

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.061
the laws

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.163
at praising

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:21.201
and and rewarding and promising to help

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.302
these people

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.469
who basically tried

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.405
to stop the peaceful transfer of power.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.005
It is

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.607
it is beyond disgraceful

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.976
and it is beyond disgraceful

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.377
that more Republicans

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.879
don't call him out for this.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:36.683
And I I'm just at a loss for words

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.318
that really adequately capture

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:41.087
how how disgusting this all is.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:42.422
And let me ask you about

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:43.656
