00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.441
basically pointing out

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:51.177
that all of the Republicans who supported

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:52.445
the charges

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.580
that wanted to Broderick

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.449
had made against Bill Clinton

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.617
back in the nineties

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.919
should be equally concerned about

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.054
and if not more concerned about

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.022
the charges

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.791
that Jean Carroll

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.426
had made against Donald Trump,

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:07.960
because there was actually

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.129
corroboration by

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.466
contemporaneous witnesses who

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.868
Jean Carroll told the story to

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.838
within days of of of it happening.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.239
And it just so happened

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:22.008
that I think the week after

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.276
I wrote that op ed,

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:26.446
I attended a party in in Manhattan,

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:28.581
just the just the dinner party

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.617
where Jean Carroll was a guest.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:32.852
And she walked up to me

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.120
and introduced herself.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.188
And I think she thanked me

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.323
for the piece that I had written.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.325
And somehow or other

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.660
she mentioned that, you know,

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.628
she had been kicking around the idea

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:43.529
of the possibility

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.464
of bringing a lawsuit

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.666
or some people were suggesting it to her.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:49.402
And I gave it about a millisecond worth

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:50.870
of thought and said, well,

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:51.337
there's a

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:52.872
there's a potential defamation claim.

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:53.706
There is a fact

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:55.374
there could be a substantial defamation

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:55.842
claim there,

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:59.278
because if he's lying about you by saying

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:00.546
that you are lying,

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.682
that is that is defamatory.

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.383
So and I said it

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:05.585
probably would make sense

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.220
if you are have any interest

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.087
in pursuing this,

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:08.988
you probably should

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.057
you should you should consult counsel.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:12.458
And then a moment later,

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.759
it popped into my head.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:16.128
Who that who that lawyer ought to be

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.764
who the right lawyer would be.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.299
A woman named Robby Kaplan,

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.868
who was a good friend of mine,

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:25.104
who is famous for having litigated

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:27.106
the Defense of Marriage Act case

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.541
